Speech
  Agent Talk's speech dependencies are installed by pip or uv, and its speech models are
  downloaded by `agent-talk setup`; none of them are part of this repository.

  GPL-3 components. Kokoro's text-to-phoneme step uses phonemizer (GPL-3.0-or-later,
  https://github.com/bootphon/phonemizer) and espeak-ng (GPL-3.0-or-later,
  https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng, shipped in the espeakng-loader wheel). Both load
  into the Agent Talk process. Agent Talk's own code remains under the Apache License 2.0,
  but a distribution that bundles Agent Talk with its speech dependencies (for example a
  container image, a system package or a frozen binary) must be offered under the terms of
  GPL-3.0.

  Parakeet TDT 0.6B v2
    Copyright NVIDIA Corporation (https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2).
    License: CC-BY-4.0. ONNX export by istupakov
    (https://huggingface.co/istupakov/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2-onnx).
  Kokoro-82M v1.0
    Copyright hexgrad (https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M). License: Apache-2.0.
    ONNX export by thewh1teagle (https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx, MIT).
    src/agent_talk/speech/kokoro_vocab.json is Kokoro-82M's phoneme vocabulary.
  Silero VAD v6.2
    Copyright Silero Team (https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad). License: MIT.
  onnx-asr (MIT), ONNX Runtime (MIT), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause).
  The `cuda` extra installs NVIDIA's CUDA and cuDNN wheels under the NVIDIA software
  license agreements that come with them.

Setup
  Rich (MIT), questionary (MIT) and prompt_toolkit (BSD-3-Clause) draw `agent-talk setup`.

Pairing
  segno (BSD-3-Clause) draws the QR codes for pairing a device.

